# The tactics screen (tactics_screens.cpp, 3; reader tel14b, the screens round, 21/11/2026): its event handler.
# tactics_screen_handle_event (0x89f710..0x8a2c5f, 13.6 KB: the whole routine hooked, written in named pieces: the
# dialog answers, the Tactics menu, Last Match, Edit and the tabs, the player list, the pitch, Cancel / Ok).
# Conventions checked in the disassembly: cdecl(short item as a dword), ret 0, returns -4 / -9 / -0xb / 0 or the
# menu bar's result; langlib_sprintf cdecl variadic (each text gets the arguments of the next call, still on the
# stack: passed the same here); confirm_push / confirm_push_text_object cdecl(7); open_file_dialog cdecl(14);
# HUMAN_MANAGER::get_folder_path thiscall ret 8, get_recent_file thiscall(6) ret 0x18, get_password ret 4;
# formation_read_file_password cdecl(4); the Tactics_Screen and Formation methods thiscall (ret = 4 x the
# arguments); bit_index_to_mask64 cdecl -> edx:eax; get_pitch_point_for_position_flags cdecl(8) (reads only the low
# byte of the flags); FIXTURE_MANAGER::find_fixtures thiscall(9) (reads only the low words of the four date
# arguments, whose high halves the original leaves with leftovers: zero here); the distance on the x87 (fild, fsqrt,
# the game's _ftol 0x945640).
# The same in the cm0102-1080.exe (whole routine).
# Needs tel14_1 (tactics_screen::*, tactics_screen_construct, tactics_screen_open, tactics_screen_free_inline,
# TACTICS_SCREENS_CPP, MATCH_TEAM_DESTRUCT_FN), tel14_2 (tactics_calls) and tel26_1 (tel26_error_box,
# tel26_item_id/_value, tel26_copy_text, display_method, display_method1, JOB_TEXT): goes after them.
# Defects of the original: Team Instructions and the player instructions read the copy's READ_ONLY (or construct)
# without checking a failed allocation; the prologue reads the club of a null object when the allocation fails; a
# player instructions screen that does not open leaks the copy; the Cancel and Ok answers (0x31, 0x32) free the
# object without clearing parameter 0.
TELAS = True
ROTINAS = [('tactics_screen_handle_event', 0x89f710, [0x6a, 0xff, 0x68, 0xfe, 0x35, 0x96, 0x00])]
DOCS = ('a tela de tática (3): os eventos',
        'the tactics screen (3): its events',
        [('tactics_screen_handle_event', 'tactics_screen_handle_event', '0x89f710', 'tactics_screens.cpp', 'cdecl',
          'trata os eventos da tela de tática: o objeto da tela (construído se falta) e as cores do uniforme do clube para as caixas. Com resposta de diálogo pendente: padrão (0x34), carregar (0x2c, o diálogo de arquivo), o arquivo a carregar (0x2d; recusado se travado pela senha de outro técnico), a tática pronta a carregar (0x36), o arquivo a salvar (0x2e), salvar como pronta (0x35), apagar (0x2f), um arquivo recente (0x30), Cancelar (0x31: libera o objeto), Ok (0x32: o capitão escolhido se o atual não está em campo, as mudanças aplicadas, o objeto liberado) e salvar antes de sair (0x33). Depois o item: Instruções do Time (uma cópia do objeto na tela delas), Cobradores de Pênalti (o elenco do clube), Padrão, Carregar, Carregar Pronta, Salvar, Salvar Como, Salvar Como Pronta, Salvar Para, Apagar, Destravar e Travar (pedem para salvar), os recentes, a coluna da Visão, Última Partida (a tática da última partida do clube nas últimas 8 semanas, 24 numa seleção, só de leitura; senão a caixa de sem partidas ou sem tática), Editar (desfazer, copiar, copiar tudo, colar, espelhar, mostrar corridas) e as abas; a lista (o número abre as instruções do jogador em campo; arrastar para a braçadeira, para os pênaltis, trocar linhas, instrução e marcação); o campo (o círculo solto na posição mais perto na visão geral ou na casa da grade 27 x 36 de maior sobreposição nas visões de zona, trocando com quem estiver lá; a posição extra; a zona clicada); Cancelar (pergunta se houve mudanças) e Ok (pergunta ao voltar à partida); o resto vai para a barra de menu. Cada mudança guarda a cópia de desfazer e marca as mudanças; a tela só de leitura não muda nada. Devolve -4, -9 (tela fechada), -0xb (redesenhar) ou 0',
          "handles the tactics screen's events: the screen object (built when missing) and the club's kit colours for the boxes. With a dialog answer pending: set to default (0x34), load (0x2c, the file dialog), the file to load (0x2d; refused when another manager's password locks it), the preset to load (0x36), the file to save (0x2e), save as preset (0x35), delete (0x2f), a recent file (0x30), Cancel (0x31: frees the object), Ok (0x32: the captain picked when the current one is not on the pitch, the changes applied, the object freed) and save before leaving (0x33). Then the item: Team Instructions (a copy of the object on their screen), Penalty Takers (the club squad), Set To Default, Load, Load Preset, Save, Save As, Save As Preset, Save For, Delete, Unlock and Lock (they ask to save), the recent files, the View column, Last Match (the tactics of the club's last match in the last 8 weeks, 24 for a national team, read-only; else the no matches or no tactics box), Edit (undo, copy, copy all, paste, reflect, show runs) and the tabs; the list (the number opens the player instructions of a player on the pitch; drags to the armband, to the penalty places, row swaps, instruction and marking); the pitch (the circle let go at the nearest position in the overview or on the cell of the 27 x 36 grid it overlaps most in the zone views, swapping with whoever is there; the extra position; the zone clicked); Cancel (asks when there are changes) and Ok (asks when going back to the match); the rest goes to the menu bar. Each change saves the undo copy and marks the changes; a read-only screen changes nothing. Returns -4, -9 (screen closed), -0xb (redraw) or 0")])
